    {
      "id": "03-fats",
      "index": 2,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "fats",
      "text": "37.1 grams of fat. Polyunsaturated fat is 5.8 grams, helping with cell structure and healthy signalling. Saturated fat is 12.6 grams, working against a cleaner fat profile, and for meats, fat quality is a major tradeoff. For meats, fat quality matters because the protein is already doing the main job.",
      "textSha256": "e7bc80b3ce58056a52a481263e9ead7a64131394ce2453b3552c203bf3f34cd1",
      "characterCount": 302,
      "byteLength": 339008,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v11-blocks/03-fats.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "WVcuekPJm7C6CSQiFTKA",
        "historyItemId": "rVhe6XmfZAiJyJReorjP"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v11-blocks/03-fats.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-carbs",
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "carbs",
      "text": "No defensible carb submacros to call out. For meats, carbs barely matter unless something has been added.",
      "textSha256": "e41017d99a46131713bc52c114c00373d9a4bad3a0cc8a2b4b14c5df928b3a6c",
      "characterCount": 105,
      "byteLength": 93248,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v11-blocks/04-carbs.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "VkkhEMvofLNTd2aMm7ag",
        "historyItemId": "hMGFTTRE4ChtPsL4xDEn"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v11-blocks/04-carbs.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-proteins",
      "index": 4,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "proteins",
      "text": "13.7 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 9 out of 9, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance. Collagen is only 0.4 grams, not adding much structural protein, so for meats, that collagen side of the protein score stays weak. For meats, protein quality is one of the biggest parts of the score.",
      "textSha256": "1ff8b6b41f1a7e13775073d23a02a36be27447c481178fabb053314fbe44ba31",
      "characterCount": 318,
      "byteLength": 345278,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v11-blocks/05-proteins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "oaOlf889oX2YQKpekEXt",
        "historyItemId": "AWpcnktec6JgtlZUQBqE"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v11-blocks/05-proteins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-vitamins",
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "vitamins",
      "text": "Vitamin B12 is 21% daily value, useful for nerve and blood-cell support. Vitamin D is only 1% daily value, not bringing much bone or immune support, so that's a small downside for meats. For meats, vitamin B12 and vitamin D are the vitamin checks that matter most.",
      "textSha256": "f1181c1303f1e628801571eb6441663b58d312c50d28d521e32502e7cfc97de7",
      "characterCount": 264,
      "byteLength": 298466,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v11-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "BuhsQtuu4YwIVhCRluCI",
        "historyItemId": "BJh3miRJkoVoQFTmGhYh"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v11-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-minerals",
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "minerals",
      "text": "Zinc is 10% daily value, useful for immune support. Iron is only 2% daily value, not bringing much oxygen-transport support. For meats, iron and zinc can add a lot beyond the protein.",
      "textSha256": "902d06e12521a6dbc2272311e1849b4f2545b6a69a6899224ae7f7745cfe6aaf",
      "characterCount": 183,
      "byteLength": 204008,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v11-blocks/07-minerals.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "Bglcsw7z174fbcYd9EKR",
        "historyItemId": "8lY7HdEuLIxDJTzQyclw"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v11-blocks/07-minerals.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-pros",
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "pros",
      "text": "Pros first: highly palatable and appealing. It is an obvious reason people like it. Works as a strong flavour booster. A small amount can carry a whole plate. Has strong comfort-food appeal. It is instantly recognisable and easy to package in meals.",
      "textSha256": "8b7fb5d22add23b69a1599d3d9c5c6bd7f987633e9d322be7f7847cd60f39b48",
      "characterCount": 249,
      "byteLength": 272135,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v11-blocks/08-pros.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "WmOfkjB7x6yu69zcLGeT",
        "historyItemId": "X14KhxS4gkuB4L5vGj7K"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v11-blocks/08-pros.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "The drawbacks next: sodium is a major drawback. Even a small serving can bring a lot of salt, so it adds up fast. Processing is a major negative. Because bacon is cured meat, the health tradeoff is bigger than the macro numbers alone suggest. Salty, fatty flavour makes portions easy to overdo. That flavour is part of the appeal, but it also makes bacon harder to keep as a small add-on.",
      "textSha256": "1887931981c0ff91104d0ca2ea8fef983d1baef6852811503a29837fda9fa9b7",
      "characterCount": 388,
      "byteLength": 401702,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v11-blocks/09-cons.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "spYTcBusMkSMnTeHlacZ",
        "historyItemId": "pkPk5ezQBnlGHhbbSMuO"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v11-blocks/09-cons.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-closing_summary",
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "closing_summary",
      "sectionKey": null,
      "text": "Big strengths are protein, palatable and appealing, and strong flavour booster, but the biggest weaknesses are low iron, low vitamin D, and saturated fat. It's good for muscles, practical meals, and blood and oxygen support because protein still gives it some muscle support, it's easy to build meals around, and vitamin B12 supports the blood-and-oxygen side.",
      "textSha256": "9b28e4fa3f5cc6be2b9a7307495e73e58d56537717218c380139783e69a64748",
      "characterCount": 360,
      "byteLength": 358653,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v11-blocks/10-closing_summary.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
